Description: port the intro from SDL 1.2 to SDL 2
 Render the software frame buffer through an SDL 2 streaming texture, with
 V-Sync. The animation is advanced once per frame, so it is also capped
 at about 60 fps in case V-Sync is not available (fast machines, high
 refresh rate screens). The window is resizable and scaled; the F key
 toggles fullscreen, and -f/--fullscreen starts in fullscreen as the
 original release did. Any other key quits.
 Also exit when the window is closed, read all pending events each frame
 (a key press could be missed) and stop reading an uninitialised event
 before the first SDL_PollEvent().
